        intro: "Acute soft-tissue injuries — sprains, strains, muscle tears within the first 42 days — progress through inflammatory, proliferative and remodeling phases. BPC-157 has been studied in rodent injury models for early angiogenesis and nitric-oxide signaling, and thymosin beta-4 (the parent of TB-500) for cell migration and anti-fibrotic effects in animal wound models. Neither has been tested in controlled human trials for acute injury. For chronic tendinopathy, post-surgical rehabilitation, or injuries beyond 6–8 weeks, see the dedicated injury-recovery page.",
